      <Abstract>
         <__mixed_content_value>
            <AbstractText>
               <__attr alias="Label" name="Label">
                  <__value>BACKGROUND</__value>
               </__attr>
               <__mixed_content_value>COPD has significant psychosocial impact. Self-management support improves quality of life, but programs are </__mixed_content_value>
               <__mixed_content_value>
                  <b>
                     <__mixed_content_value>not </__mixed_content_value>
                     <__mixed_content_value>
                        <u>
                           <__mixed_content_value>universally</__mixed_content_value>
                        </u>
                     </__mixed_content_value>
                     <__mixed_content_value> available</__mixed_content_value>
                  </b>
               </__mixed_content_value>
               <__mixed_content_value>. IT-based self- management interventions can provide home-based support, but have mixed results. </__mixed_content_value>
               <__mixed_content_value>
                  <i>
                     <__mixed_content_value>We conducted a case</__mixed_content_value>
                  </i>
               </__mixed_content_value>
               <__mixed_content_value> series of an off-the- shelf Internet</__mixed_content_value>
               <__mixed_content_value>
                  <sup>
                     <__mixed_content_value>-based</__mixed_content_value>
                  </sup>
               </__mixed_content_value>
               <__mixed_content_value> health</__mixed_content_value>
               <__mixed_content_value>
                  <sub>
                     <__mixed_content_value>-promotion</__mixed_content_value>
                  </sub>
               </__mixed_content_value>
               <__mixed_content_value> program, The Preventive Plan (TPP), coupled with Nurse-coach support, which aimed to increase patient activation and provide </__mixed_content_value>
               <__mixed_content_value>
                  <sub>
                     <__mixed_content_value>self-management</__mixed_content_value>
                  </sub>
               </__mixed_content_value>
               <__mixed_content_value> benefits. </__mixed_content_value>
            </AbstractText>
         </__mixed_content_value>
         <__mixed_content_value>
            <AbstractText>
               <__attr alias="Label" name="Label">
                  <__value>METHODS</__value>
               </__attr>
               <__mixed_content_value>A total of </__mixed_content_value>
               <__mixed_content_value>
                  <b>
                     <__mixed_content_value>
                        <i>
                           <__mixed_content_value>19 COPD patients</__mixed_content_value>
                        </i>
                     </__mixed_content_value>
                  </b>
               </__mixed_content_value>
               <__mixed_content_value> were recruited, and 14 completed 3-month follow-up in two groups: </__mixed_content_value>
               <__mixed_content_value>
                  <b>
                     <__mixed_content_value>groups </__mixed_content_value>
                     <__mixed_content_value>
                        <i>
                           <__mixed_content_value>
                              <b>
                                 <__mixed_content_value>1 and 2</__mixed_content_value>
                              </b>
                           </__mixed_content_value>
                           <__mixed_content_value> or 3</__mixed_content_value>
                        </i>
                     </__mixed_content_value>
                     <__mixed_content_value> with </__mixed_content_value>
                     <__mixed_content_value>
                        <b>
                           <__mixed_content_value>more and less</__mixed_content_value>
                        </b>
                     </__mixed_content_value>
                     <__mixed_content_value> advanced COPD</__mixed_content_value>
                  </b>
               </__mixed_content_value>
               <__mixed_content_value>, respectively. Change in patient activation was determined with paired t-tests and Wilcoxon signed-rank tests. Benefits and user experience were explored in semistructured interviews, analyzed thematically.</__mixed_content_value>
            </AbstractText>
         </__mixed_content_value>
         <__mixed_content_value>
            <AbstractText>
               <__attr alias="Label" name="Label">
                  <__value>RESULTS</__value>
               </__attr>
               <__mixed_content_value>Only group 1 improved significantly in activation, from a lower baseline than group 2; group 1 also improved significantly in mastery and anxiety. Both groups felt significantly more informed about COPD and reported physical functioning improvements. Group 1 reported improvements in mood and confidence. Overall, group 2 reported fewer benefits than group 1. Both groups valued nurse-coach support; for group 1, it was more important than TPP in building confidence to self-manage. The design of TPP and lack of motivation to use IT were barriers to use, but disease severity and poor IT skills were not. </__mixed_content_value>
            </AbstractText>
         </__mixed_content_value>
         <__mixed_content_value>
            <AbstractText>
               <__attr alias="Label" name="Label">
                  <__value>DISCUSSION</__value>
               </__attr>
               <__mixed_content_value>Our findings demonstrate the feasibility of combining nurse-coach support aligned to an Internet-based health resource, TPP, in COPD and provide learning about the challenges of such an approach and the importance of the nurse-coach role.</__mixed_content_value>
            </AbstractText>
         </__mixed_content_value>
      </Abstract>
      <OtherAbstract>
         <__attr alias="Sprache" name="Language">
            <__value>eng</__value>
         </__attr>
         <__attr alias="Type" name="Type">
            <__value>plain-language-summary</__value>
         </__attr>
         <__mixed_content_value>An important part of managing COPD is self-management by the patient. With IT-based self-management programs, patients can do this from their own home, which is easier for them and more cost-effective for the health care provider. Our goal was to explore how a generic Internet-based health-promotion program, The Preventive Plan (TPP), containing programs to support behavior change and health information, combined with support from a specialist nurse, could help patients to manage their COPD... Our findings demonstrate that a low-intensity intervention can produce meaningful benefits, and provides learning about the challenges of this approach and the importance of the nurse coach role. </__mixed_content_value>
      </OtherAbstract>
